schedule contention stage: unlocked
schedule contention stage: locked
schedule contention: every online core claiming one Ready process, the race shown without the lock and gone with it ok
pid contention stage: unlocked
pid contention stage: locked
pid contention: every online core minting, the counter advanced once per round unlocked and once per call locked ok
fd refcount contention stage: complete
fd refcount contention: every online core retaining and releasing one object, count back to baseline ok
asid contention stage: complete
asid contention: every online core assigning, every number advanced the counter once ok
page contention stage: complete
page contention: every online core allocating and freeing, every page back, none freed twice ok
freelist contention stage: unlocked
freelist contention stage: locked
freelist contention: unlocked hands one index to every online core, a caller's lock stops it ok
pool contention stage: complete
pool contention: every online core cycling one pool, every allocation given back, no handle refused ok
occupancy drain stage: complete
occupancy drain: every online peer held the region and each bounded drain gave up until the last had left, then the same drain handed over a proof ok
world stop counts: full=1 partial=1 resumed=1 inspections=1 repeated=16 busy=16 stale-refused=1
world stop: full token stopped and resumed every online peer, partial token refused non-acknowledging peers ok
stopped root publication: consecutive stop captures retain usable roots ok
stopped pool inspection: VM, image, FD context and descriptor metadata refused while their guards were held ok
network init contention counts: unlocked=every-online-core locked=1
network init contention: unlocked check-set minted on every online core, typed one-shot gate admitted one initializer ok
tcp fixture claim contention counts: unlocked=every-online-core data=64 fin=64 syn-ack=64
tcp fixture claim contention: unlocked check-clear taken on every online core, each armed drop claimed once per round ok
tcp owner contention counts: busy=every-peer advanced=every-peer
tcp owner contention: every peer excluded while held and each completed one state transition after release ok
tcp pin cost evidence: 7 samples of 4096 operations and checksums consumed ok
tcp pool cost evidence: all online cores completed every lock and owner sample ok
pin sharing evidence: same-chunk layouts checked, every online core completed and the page returned ok
pool walk stage: complete
pool walk: a walk's reference to a record freed under it is refused, and the floor reads back ok
ext2 mutation contention reader: control-overlap=every-peer waited-overlap=0
ext2 mutation contention core0 reader: control-overlap=1 waited-overlap=0
ext2 mutation contention stage: complete
ext2 mutation contention counts: asked=every-peer-twice clear=every-peer held=every-peer
ext2 mutation contention: every peer is told no mutation is in flight while core 0 holds nothing, told there is one while it holds the guard, and a mutation on any core waits for readers already inside on the others ok
signal contention: every online core setting and clearing pending signal bits lost updates with a forged guard and none under the process-run lock ok
world stop from a peer counts: complete=every-peer
world stop from a peer: every peer in turn began a stop of every online core and the others acknowledged it ok
